From 29eb8560705165dc5b19adfaa2f65dfbbd9af558 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rainer Gerhards <rgerhards@adiscon.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:27:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] queue: destroy completed messages under the queue mutex again

Why:
Unlocked disposal from 454b340a1 costs ~40% more CPU and ~12% less
throughput on JSON-heavy rulesets with several queue workers, see
https://github.com/rsyslog/rsyslog/issues/7884

Impact: classic queue workers free completed batches under the mutex.
Before/After: concurrent unlocked frees -> serialized frees in lock.

Technical Overview:
With deferred disposal, every worker frees its batch concurrently
right after unlocking. perf shows the frees from msgDestruct() and
the mallocs from scriptExec() of the next batch fighting for the same
glibc arena lock: futex calls grew from ~320k to ~7M per run.
Classic (non-local) queues now destroy the batch in
qqueueDisposeBatch() under the queue mutex, as before 454b340a1, so
their deferred buffer stays empty and the drain calls are no-ops.
Local queue backends keep their own deferred disposal unchanged.
Drop queue-deferred-idle-wakeup.sh, queue-deferred-idle-shutdown.sh
and their interposer: they assert unlocked classic disposal.
The cancellation and idle shutdown rechecks from 454b340a1 stay.

With the help of AI-Agents: Claude Code

